</figure>
<div id="S4.SS2.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We further analyze the distribution of attack styles selected by Red-Bandit in the ASR@10 setting across proprietary models and Llama-3.1-8B (Table <a href="#S4.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ 4.2.3 Identifying Attack-Style Vulnerabilities ‣ 4.2 Results ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Red-Bandit: Test-Time Adaptation for LLM Red-Teaming via Bandit-Guided LoRA Experts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>). This analysis reveals which adversarial styles each model is most vulnerable to and how different bandit policies adapt their exploration strategies. Interestingly, each model exhibits distinct susceptibility patterns: Llama-3.1-8B is sensitive to hypothetical and authority-manipulation attacks, GPT-4o is most affected by historical and role-play scenarios, while GPT-3.5-turbo shows higher vulnerability to uncommon dialects and hypothetical reasoning. The <math id="S4.SS2.SSS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-greedy policy tends to focus on a few dominant attack styles, whereas UCB maintains a more balanced distribution across multiple styles. These results suggest that Red-Bandit not only maximizes attack success but also exposes model-specific weaknesses in the attack-style space, providing a useful diagnostic tool for understanding model vulnerabilities.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.3 </span>Ablation Studies</h3>

<section id="S4.SS3.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">4.3.1 </span>Impact of RL Post-Training and Bandits</h4>

<figure id="S4.T4" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S4.T4.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 4</span>: </span><span id="S4.T4.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
Ablation study against the Llama3.1-8B target. We report ASR@1 under keyword matching,
normalized style entropy (<math id="S4.T4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{\text{norm}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mtext>norm</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{\text{norm}}</annotation></semantics></math>), and perplexity (PPL) measured with Mistral-7B reference model.
Best results are in <span id="S4.T4.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">bold</span>.
</span></figcaption>
<table id="S4.T4.6" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
